# FogHTTP response streaming benchmark results

- Timestamp: `{{ timestamp }}`
- Python: `{{ python_version }}`
- Platform: `{{ platform_name }}`
- Server: `local asyncio HTTP/1.1 loopback server`
- Measurement scope: `shared-client-server-process-v1`; resource peaks include the local server and harness and are incomparable with separate-PID client resources.
- Metric schema: `2`; EOF throughput scope `verified-eof-v2`, timing scope `load-only-v2`.
- Duration covers load, consumer counting, incremental SHA-256 and finalization for full bytes streams, and response-context exit. Sampler setup/teardown, client close and reporting are excluded.
- Built-in full bytes cases use deterministic `byte-pattern-0-255-v1` content and require matching status, size, EOF and SHA-256. Text/lines retain their size/line checks.
- Observed totals include completed invalid outcomes; a raised client exception can hide partial bytes from this legacy adapter API. Failed and expected early-close responses contribute zero verified EOF bytes and zero EOF MiB/s.
- Streams/run: `{{ args.requests }}`
- Warmup/run: `{{ args.warmup }}`
- Repeats: `{{ args.repeats }}`
- Shuffle seed: `{{ args.seed }}`

